        <p>LADIES will be glad to heir that Mrs. M. Darnerau, CERTIFICATED MIDWIFE, has a safe and certain mixture for obstructions and irregularities, which she will send, post free, for 4s. 9d. It is absolutely guwanteed, even in long.st uding obstinate cases. It cannot fail, and is perfectly harmless. Do not trust in bogus advertisements of quacks and other ignorant people, they never send you the right remedy. It you have already done so, send for this Mixture as a last resource, and you will not be deceived. You will find that it is always cheaper to come to the right place first. Below are Some testimonials received. The originals of these, with thousands of others, can be seen any time. From Mrs. CI. Sham : "Medlin, will you kindly send again one bottle f your Female Mixture, as the last acted splendidly. I enclose &amp;c."—Mrs. Binnze writes : " Kindly jorward by return of et a bottle of your Female Mixture. It put me all rigle last oirne, and I trust it will do so again." —From Mrs. )lecher t "Madame, I received the Mixture all right, and I took the doses as stated ; it did all that was needed, for which I thank you very much."—Mrs, S. writes from Sheffield: "I em pleased to tell you your medicine did all that was required, though I thought it bad failed, for I had the last dose thirty hours before any change took place. I had the last dose on Sunday, and all was right as possible Tuesday afternoon. Everything had been as well as It Wall possible. Had I written toyou at first, I should have been over £2 in pocket. You may show this letter, but cover name and address."—Mrs. Bryan writes: "Madam, am glad to be able to report that the last two doses have ad the desired effect. I shall recommend your remedy to It my married friends. I think it is excellent, and should be in difficulty again myself, should at once apply to you." —From Mrs Garside : " I have much pleasure in sending you news of haying relief the first morning, for which lam • very thankful indeed. I shall always feel grateful for your Mixture, and if I need anything again, will send to y0u.".4 Address: Mae. DAMBRAU, Milton Cottage, Forest Hill, London</p>
