        <p>Tho above Council held its usual fortnightly meeting st the Dutton Workhouse. on Tuesday. There being Present :—Messre. J. Knowles, J.P. (chairman). Samuel Woodward (vice-chaitmati),E. Clarke. J. Weir,T. L9llB, t, Mclntyre. T. Ant wiss. Peter Leather, J. Stlkes, W. clrering, W.7leteher. c. E. Linaker. J. G. Kydd, H. +alba, T. Baxter, T. Darlington. E. Brethertoo, T, u,Weight, J. B. Chadwick. with Mr. John Ashton (clerk). /1" • George A,loton (claouty-clmk). Mr. J. Farrington 'llslPector), Mr. R. Diggle and Mr. Swinton (Surveyors), Dr. Adams (medical officer.) TELEGRAPH OFFICE AT STRETTON. The Secretary of the General Post Office, London, for- Ijarded for execution under tae common seal of the Uücll copies of the deed of agreement with the Depart. tient for a telegraph office at Stratton.—The deed was Itecuted.</p>
