        <p>RUNCORN BOARD OF GUARDIANS.</p>
        <p>The fortnightly meeting of this Board was held at Dutton Workhouse on Tuesday. There Were present : Mr. J. Stokes (in the chair), Messrs. A. H. Norman, J. Meadowcroft, T. Lea, S. Mir wood, the memb of the Rural District Council, with Mr. J. Ashton (clerk) and Mr. Y. F. Ashton (deputy clerk): AMMO WLE D OMEN I% MiS3 EtzaAndrews, Runcorn, wro:e aoknowled;ing receipt of intim Won thit she hal been electel upon the ladies Visiting Ountnittee.</p>
        <p>TRANSFER OF A PAUPER. Mr. Albart E. &amp;loiter, clerk to the Shsffield Board of Guardians, wrote under date August 31, 1893, re 8 ,muel Pickering (14) as f snows : The abova n imed was admitted to the children's Homes of tole Union yesterday, an as he was only ramoved to your wo,k- house in darch last. I shall bo obliged it you will tavJur ins with an order for his re-admission.—The order was granted.</p>
