        <p>FINANCIAL MATTIMS.-THE ESTIM&amp;TE.</p>
        <p>Mr. Woodward r that the amoues graate I fo out-relief were :—Ruoco-o astrict £B5 ; Frodsham £24; and Bud wo t'a £22. The paynclats that da7 aimeuMed to £134 16i., leaving a ' balance of £1,624 9i 101. report was adopted.—Mr. Woo ward also submitted th etimate of expenditure for the half year ending Lady Day 1899. Tao peobLb;e espeoliture was as futiewa ; Common cicarges, £2.190 ; county rate. £3 437 ; b tlanc and contingeicy fund. £2,150; total £7,777. Alter deduct .ng the nr bable balance in favour of parishes at Michaele:las 1898, the amount required by contribu;lon 'orders fr )no•4vars.ierA gni £5,808. Toe asmseab e VALUO of the Union WAR £203,494. rate. of 611 ia the '£ would proluce £5,590. It was recommsnde 1 tat cal for this sum be inade.—The es:incate was adop'aef as read. , DECOEUTION OF THE BOARD-ROOM. The following tender was accepted f &gt;r tne decoration of the Board Room, a -,c3rding to the specifications su,e- mitterl by the srahiteet (Mr. Davies) Jame; Green, Church-street, Runcorn, for £lO 123 61.—Mr. UnalcAr cpeouonel the wiiid )in of prooedig with the work until the walls were thoroughly dry, but af:er some:diseussion the work was decided to be p:ccieled with.</p>
        <p>THE REPRESENTATION OF CENTRAL WARD, RUNCORN. Notice of a vacancy in Central Ward, due to the fact that Mr. Samuel Yarwood (who was e`ected as its repre- sentative), but who has been °olio,' to sit for the re• Presentation of Newton War i was g;van bY Mosses. S. Yar wood and T. Lea (both Guardians of the Runcorn The Clerk stated that the election would be proceeded with in due course. This concluded the business.</p>
