        <p>ATHLETIC SPORTS,</p>
        <p>------ -- The third W.:Matto meettng in connection with the Runcorn Fo°than Club took place on the Irwell-iane Enclosure on Saturday afternoon. The idea of holding a second meeting this year emanated from Mr. Albert Abel, the assistant secr3tary of toe club, who.uadertriok all responsibility. The weather was all that could be desired, and the enterprise was liberally supported by the townspeople and a good contingent from Widnes and surrounding places. There were about 300 entries ani, with five exceptions, the competitors were resident in the district. Toe 220 yards handicap for media era of the Ruecora F )(Abell Club, and the tug-of.war proved the most exciting evens. Dur;ng the afternoon tie Runcorn Voltmeer Bind disc Airs ed some excel:en', music under the direction of Bandmaster Outhwaite. The principal offizisla in connection with th Sports were : Judgee, Measrs. T. C. Cooper, J. Tudor, G. Robinson, S. C. Haddock, W. E. Lancaster, G. Maeki3 ; handl- cattp.r, H. P. Ellis, Official handicapp-r, Liverpool ; timekeeper and referee, G. Wainwright ; starter, W. Jones; sports hon..vcs., A. Abel and J. Ellison ; hon. treasurer, C. Pownall. Appended are details :- 123 Yards Flat Race Handicap (Loos.l).—Winnors of heats : W B Hough, Runcorn, s.ft yards; W Cooper, Ruacorn, 3} yards ; P bee. Widnes, six yi.rds ; F White,Widnes, 1 yards; J Moran, Weston, 4 yards; A flayter, Runcorn, 5 yards. Final: 1, P Ince; 2. a Moran ; 3, W. H flough. The first man won by about a yard. and the seeoud by inches only. 833 Yards Handicap (EaSea.O.-1, A D Mather, Widnes, 5 yards ; 2, T Kargels, Widnes. 43 yard,; 3. G Wright, Widnes watch. Id ither won by aboat tour yarda,while about a yard divided Oa second and third. Tug of War.—the draw was as follows ;-114alehurst'5 Co. v Wigg's U.A. ; A. 8.0. Co. Sprinch yard v Castner-Kellner Works ; Gosiagas v Runcorn Docks M.S.C. Co) ; Ookleston's Works, a bye. The suoceisful isompetitara la the first roan I were :—Wlizg's Works Gaither Kellner and Runcorn Docks. In the second round Wigg's be it Ockleston's. The final between Wigg's and Caslner-K liners yrs, a very tough strianle, the prince event sally going to the erupt .iyiSs of Whig's Works. 120 Yards Handle (Open).—Winners of heats : 3 W Rains, !databank, 14 yards; W Clapton, Crewe, 9} yards ; Rose, Thornton, AC. llk y trots ; H Kent, Runs wa.lol yards; J Moran, Weston. 12 yards ; A Wool ey, Boughton &amp;C., tot yards. Final 1, W Clanton ;2. S Ross; 3, H Kent. Runcorn. Capton woo by about half a yard, and there was a differeace of a yard between the second and third. 220 Yards Handicap. —o,infined to members of Runcorn Football Club. The c smpetitor3 ran in football oosturne, First Hest : 1, S Houghton, ten yards; 3, W;lte2e,cwa. 7 yards. S eSet„ ytonAirdh,e.atT:hirli. Jheaßutt,tel. rwaorritha.yttehrresetx yards yards 2. S Walker nine yards. Fourth heat: 1. Faulkner, eight yards :2; , Y itestic y rls. Final: 1, J Faulkner; 2, Houghton 8 Walker.44o Yards Obstacle Race Handicap. —Firat heat 1, w Mitchell. Id A. 0, scratol ; 2, 3 Hoofer. Farnworth Harriers scratch; 3, A Beddow, Middidton, 10 yards. Second heat 1, AS A Mitshell Ii AO, 5 yards; 2, A Brenthim, Newtown. ' . screch ;3. J Sweene, W'idnes. 20 yards. Final: .ILinkerklker : 2, A. J A Mitchell ; 3, W J 220 Yards Handicap (Open) —Winners of beam; w Clapton, Crewe, 13 yards ; p Ines, Widnes. 16 yards ; A. WooleY, Broughton AC.. 14 yards; J Wolfe. Crewe Harriers, 14 yar is ; H Kent. it Incorn. 15 yards. Final: 1, W Clapron ; 2, 11 Kant ;3, P fuse. °lepton wan by about belt a yard. One Mile Haniicap.-1, It Mestere, Crewe S.U.C., 138 yards 2, T Hughes, Widnes, 125 yards ;3. G Wright, Wid. nes, 105 yards. Of:esters won easily.</p>
