        <p>_ The monthly rneoting of ots Council was held at the Town Hall on 'Nos Soy-Alderman Sadler (Deputy Mayor) presiding. Toe totc,diasc Officer of Health reported that 94 births and 53 deaths had isocurred in the borough doing the past m oath. Thirtv•four oases of typhoid had Win nstified, as against 12 in the correspoudiwz o cnudr rarsdh, p withitn itn the rne exceptiontntety b t month of last year. Twenty-sight 'cases were ramovc•cl Ito the hospital,w' rn nilst six were treated at itoe. All the • 'houses akadb waicihni a) hpetnhep rfieviiprivies considerable number ef Instncee the liqui 1 contents kept oozing through the im perfectly constructed privy "allga fouling the back yards and oausisg abouoinable smells Councillor Nail, in moving the . minutes of the tlealtio Committee, said that the outb -ea' mortared to be diminishi ig, judging from the numb .r of •nolfloa- dons. He only wished the proper,trowaers would give as much attention to tho backs of the houses .as they did to the front.—A resolution of the Gas and Water Com- mittee, that tho Town Clerk be instructed to make appli- t the lageatsiowno r ktos cote of Les, cation to e OsL, rifhcanaenrl odflor ntvhe,erirn regulationsaei opxnanerton 48. ifenoodat: rs, of aefato mar anagemont of atownonri oewa alsoe Er t4era, ,!iO. Ponc-d to open the cemoterV 2t was P 27th but sevora' m hnbers objected until the q onstion of consecratitn had been tt ho e t formally isas e a: 0e::y the I sh Vet ; and Ald irmaa Williams, challn in of the Cern-- tery Coonnittee agre hi to take the minwe b .ck. The Dapul-Mayor said tins could not he -lone without the to 9 to open the cchnetery on the above date.—Couneilic,,• cifoenmsc:unteowfatvbe: Coalto_ancili,swahf bnitt'soefly3.,sdnitheoiairitapheedopprbeaic Deputy-Mayor said he had no desire to bustle ths matter through,and again put the motto to poes:pavoneextphreesospeedna- ing, only 5 now voting for it.—The preposition was, hopstherefore, tba. nee% rr Churchmen.— Couo cwi 1