        <head>VESUVIUS IN ERUPTION.</head>
        <p>VESUVIUS IN ERUPTION.</p>
        <p>THREITENED DESIRUCTION OF PROPERTY. ROME. THURSDAY.</p>
        <p>Telegrams from Naples state that a .is'-ree.-an-o-rlsa.va from Vesuvius has d.,tcoyei port of the ral way Ind- ira:: from the observatory to the lower station f the Funicular railway. A mass of moulten rock is flowing down the mountain side in three imposing straams, one a'ong the foot ef Motole Sonoma. a second through the middle of the Vetrana Lone, and a third along Monte Crocella. The stream running round the base of Monte Somme continues to burn the chestaut wco is, and nearly reaches the observatory. The central flow has reached a point close to the Carabinecr Barracks, while the Crocella stream, after passing c'ose to Messrs. Cook and Sons' building, has reached the northern edge of the Canteroni ridge, whence it may also threaten the obser- vatory.</p>
        <p>_ A SHARK ON THE EAST COAST. KILLED BY A WOMAN. The Press Ameiation states that at Hoanhatn,Norfolk, on Wednesday evening. ahg flit] cline close inshore, and Mrs. Harry Pope killed it with thv aid of a piece of wood. The fish proved to to a hark, eight feet two inehes long and four f.et in girth in the thickest part.</p>
