        <p>NEW FEATURE IN THE "EXIMIMER OF SEPTEMBER 30,H, 1898. We are pleased to announce that on the above date we shall commence a weekly DRAUGHTS COLUMN, which will be SPECIALLY WRITTEN FOR THE " EXAMIMER," BY A THOROUGHLY COMPETENT LOCAL PLAYER. The column will contain REPORTS of and CO BI- MEETS on all the matches in the WARRINGTON DRAUGHTS LEAGUE, together with Diagrams of GAMES AND PROBLEM POSITIONS, which have arisen in these matcbes, or which may suggeA themselves to the Draughts Editor. Everybody who takes an interest in the game of Draughts should certainly obtain a copy of the " EXAMIMER " OF SEPTEMBER 30TH. The " Examiner" cm be had, post free, for a period of twelve months fore sum of 6s. 6n. or may be purchased weekly for Id.</p>
        <p>NEW STORY IN THE EXAMINER, SEFIEMBER 30TH, 1898. We have great pleasure in announcing that we have made arrangements to puhlli.h A NEW AND THRILLING STORY of LOVE, WAR, AND ADVENTURE. The Entitled— THE SECRET OF MARK PETS,' and is from the pen of MR. FRED J. PROCTOR, The author of many popnlar works. Including "Timothy Twill's Secret,"" Jean Marlou, ' • Dr. Dodds," etc. " THE SECRET OF MARK PEPYS deals with life in the pastoral age of California. The plot is of a striking character, skilfully evolved with a sensational climax. Everyone mould read THE SECRET OF' MARE PUTS,' BY FRED J. PROCTOR. The opening chapters will appear in our columns on SEPTEMBER 30TH, 1898•</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON SCHOOL OF ART EXHIBITION, 4 SELECTION from the sUCCESSFUL WORKS admitted t/ the Science and Art Department to the NATIONAL t43I4PETITION for Medals and Prizes will I e exhibited at We rington School of Art OP THURSDAY. 15th, to be'SDAY, 19th September inclusive. The Exhibition will „Pben from 10 a.m. to 9 p.m. each d .y. Admission free. JaiE SESSION will coma ence Tuesday,September 20th CHARLES MADEL EY, Secretary.</p>
